The bug is that the loop condition uses `i <= items.length`, which causes the loop to run one extra time, beyond the last index of the array. This results in an out-of-bounds access when `i` equals `items.length`.

Here is the corrected version:

```javascript
function last(items) {
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
    if (items[i]) return items[i];
  }
}
```
